    "text": "WDAM-TV\nwebsite\nShelby\nOldest building at Shelby becomes newest museum exhibit\nBy Charles Herrington,\n8 hours agoCAMP SHELBY, Miss. (WDAM) - The oldest building at Camp Shelby is the newest exhibit at the Mississippi Armed Forces Museum. The structure, known as the Engineers’ Arsenal, was built back in 1917 to hold fuses and detonating caps for an engineer battalion. It’s the only surviving building left...\n1",
